  "query_preview": "..\nKEY MESSAGE 1...\n\nMuch colder air filters in behind the cold front tonight, with \na few snow flakes or wintry mix likely in the mtns. Even a \ndusting of snow will be possible across the highest peaks by \nearly Sunday morning. \n\nWhile temperatures will dip below 36 for some locales, \nclouds/wind should negate any frost development. A better \nchance is for the mtns and some foothill locations Sunday night \ninto Monday morning, where a Freeze Watch was issued. There \ncould be an expansion of frost/freeze headlines, especially for \nportions of SE OH, but confidence is too low at this time. There\ncould also be more snow showers for the mtns Sunday night into\nMonday, with light accumulations on the higher peaks.  \n\nAnother round of frost/freeze, which will be more widespread is\nexpected Monday night into Tuesday. This will likely impact \nlowland locations with an increasing likelihood of headlines. \n\nKEY MESSAGE 2...\n\nDaily min RHs will be in the 20s/30s percent range Sunday\nthrough Tuesday. A few disturbances will swing by the area, \nhopefully providing some relief to suppress fire danger in \ncertain areas, however these disturbances look very minor and \nmuch of the area will likely not receive any rainfall. With a \ngood wetting expected today into Sunday hopefully that will \nrefrain the fire danger threat for at least into Monday. \nRegardless, this setup will have to be closely monitored on a \ndaily basis and collaborated with local partners to see if any \nspecial weather statements will be needed.",
